# Commits and pushes

Before **any** `git commit` or `git push`, **read** `Conventional Commits.md` at the repo root (use the Read tool). Do not write a message from memory of this rule or of `AGENTS.md`. Follow that file, then continue.

If the request is only to push, still read it and check that commits already on the branch match it (no `wip`, `test123`, mixed `feat`+`fix`).

Do not skip this because the message looks obvious or because a previous turn already committed.